{"result":[{"biographic_references":[],"contributors":{"authors":[{"aliases":[],"checked":"1","codes":["zhu.xuding"],"name":"Zhu, Xuding"}],"author_references":[],"editors":[]},"database":"Zbl","datestamp":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","document_type":{"code":"j","description":"journal article"},"editorial_contributions":[{"language":"English","reviewer":{"author_code":"scapellato.raffaele","reviewer_id":"6538","name":"Raffaele Scapellato","sign":"Raffaele Scapellato (Milano)"},"text":"Let \\(G\\) and \\(H\\) be graphs. An \\(H\\)-coloring of \\(G\\) is a mapping \\(f:V(G)\\to V(H)\\) such that \\(f(x)f(y)\\in E(H)\\) if \\(xy\\in E(G)\\). (A proper \\(n\\)-coloring is the special case where \\(H=K_n\\).) A graph \\(H\\) is a core if \\(H\\) is not \\(H'\\)-colorable for all proper subgraphs \\(H'\\) of \\(H\\). A graph \\(G\\) is uniquely \\(H\\)-colorable if there is a surjective \\(H\\)-coloring of \\(G\\), that is unique up to automorphisms of \\(H\\). It is shown that if the chromatic number \\(\\chi(G)\\) is large enough (depending on \\(H)\\) then the categorical product \\(H\\times G\\) is uniquely \\(H\\)-colorable. This generalizes a known result of \\textit{D. Greenwell} and \\textit{L. Lovász} [Acta Math. Acad. Sci. Hung. 25, 335-340 (1974; Zbl 0294.05108)] stating that \\(K_n\\times G\\) is uniquely \\(n\\)-colorable if \\(\\chi (G) >n\\). A new construction of \\(n\\)-colorable triangle-free graphs is also given.","contribution_type":"review"}],"id":1309148,"identifier":"0937.05043","keywords":[],"language":{"languages":["English"],"addition":[null]},"license":[],"links":[{"identifier":"10.1002/(SICI)1097-0118(199901)30:1<1::AID-JGT1>3.0.CO;2-P","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/(SICI)1097-0118(199901)30:1<1::AID-JGT1>3.0.CO;2-P"}],"msc":[{"code":"05C15","scheme":"msc2020","text":"Coloring of graphs and hypergraphs"}],"references":[{"doi":null,"position":"1","text":"Bondy, J Graph Theory 14 pp 479-- (1990)","zbmath":{"author_codes":[],"document_id":